cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the paper below and the software."
title: "leaf-conductance: boundary-layer conductance of leaves under free, forced and mixed convection (Python and MATLAB)"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-12
license: GPL-3.0
authors:
  - family-names: Graefe
    given-names: Jan
    affiliation: Leibniz Institute of Vegetable and Ornamental Crops (IGZ), Grossbeeren, Germany
repository-code: https://github.com/Code4Plants/leaf-conductance
abstract: >-
  Free convection after Graefe, Grosch & Bitterlich (2022) for inclined elliptical leaves,
  extended by laminar forced convection along the wind streamlines, the laminar-turbulent
  transition (Lienhard 2020), a parsimonious angle-of-attack model fitted to 815 literature
  measurements, mixed convection and side-specific conductances for heat, water vapour and CO2.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "The boundary layer conductance of inclined elliptical leaves under free convection"
  authors:
    - family-names: Graefe
      given-names: Jan
    - family-names: Grosch
      given-names: Rita
    - family-names: Bitterlich
      given-names: Michael
  journal: Agricultural and Forest Meteorology
  volume: 317
  year: 2022
  doi: 10.1016/j.agrformet.2022.108884
